The bverreau@mipos2.UUCP (stargazer) writes:
=> In case there's still time to fix some of the more blatant "cheats", might I
=> suggest that in 3.0 you
=> 
=> . Disallow unlimited polymorphing piles of objects, in particular, the
=>   trick that lets you get any number of wands of wishing you want.

I thot that was already taken care of in 2.3.  You can polymorph up
all the wands of wishing you want, but they won't have any charges.

=> . Make it much harder to steal from shopkeepers.

Well, at least one trick is less likely to work now.

=> . Reduce the benefits of praying.

In 3.0, praying is not very effacious when you are not at an altar.

=> . Make it harder to maximize your luck.

The sacrifice thing is quite fixed.  However, you'll probably need all
the luck you can get.

=> . No more dipping weapons in potions of sickness to increase enchantment,
=>   especially if they can later be polymorphed into something wieldable.

Perhaps we could just prevent you from dipping large things like 2-h
swords and quarterstaffs and such.  Or limit it to swords and ammo.
Bears consideration.

=> . And, of course, Death to Elbereth!

By the option of the local wizard.

=> But, on the other hand, I would very much enjoy seeing a new user option -
=> "killdog" - which allows you to kill your stupid mutt without penalty.

No.  Just abandon it on level 1 if you want to be rid of it.  There is
a "safe_dog" option now which prevents you from hitting your dog
without even asking you, and otherwise "confirm" asks you.  You can
still attack your dog if you really want to.


